  "worked_solution": "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the origin is \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $(0,0)$ and has radius $r=3.$ So, the equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={3}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
